. You're better off aiming for \"All Chows\" (2 points) + possible \"Mixed Shifted Chows\" (6 points) or \"Mixed Triple Chow\" (8 points) if structured well. Keeping multiple singles like J1/J2/J3 hinders progress.\n\nReason: Discarding J1 removes a loose honor tile that is less likely to complete an opponent\u2019s hand (due to prior exposure), while allowing you to focus on developing chows in the Bamboo suit. It maintains safety and improves hand efficiency toward a potentially scoring pattern.\n\nAnswer: Play J1"}
